 (∆style ∆border)←((1↓¨arg),⊂⍬)[actions⍳'style' 'border']
 ∆border←(0=≢∆border)⌈×+/∊∆border ⋄ ∆style←##._supp.SetBitVals ∆style
 arg←(parent:parent ⋄ border:∆border)##.##.New.Center arg
 props←'SubForm'('Visible' 0) ⍝ Set standard creation properties
 props,←⊂'Border'∆border ⍝ Set border upon creation ⍝? Create-only
 props,←⊂'VScroll'(-16∊∆style) ⍝ Create-only
 props,←⊂'HScroll'(-64∊∆style) ⍝ Create-only
 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object
 newobj._imagesize←_size ⍝ Set default size (in scaled units; in case it's never set)
 px←⌊0.5+_size×1⌷3⊃##._supp.MyUnits parent ⍝ Assume defult size in pixels (in case it's never set)
 newobj ##.##.∆WS('Coord' 'User')('YRange'(0,px[1]))('XRange'(0,px[2])) ⍝ Special case which the Picture needs for Zooming and Scrolling
⍝? Note: Make sure that ##.Size & friends don't mess with Coord=User objects (I don't think they will)
⍝? How can we exclude scroll bars from this(??) sizing process? May have to work with ##.size & family (and without breaking anything else)??

 props←⊂'Bitmap'
 bkg←256⊥3⍴240 ⍝ Default background color (before being able to set its own 'color')
 props,←⊂'CBits'(px⍴bkg) ⍝ Start with a blank screen by default (it will get overwritten entirely if there is bitmap or image data)
 newpic←⎕VGET(newobj⍕⍛,'._pic')##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the hidden Dyalog object to hold the dynamic image
 ##.##.New.InitChild newobj newpic

⍝ Must do this after creating the child because argument-processing will depend on it
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure
 newobj ##.##.∆WS'Picture'(newpic 0) ⍝? Will the SubForm auto-update when the Bitmap's CBits are changed (explicitly or implicitly)?


