⍝? Questions:
⍝? What happens in APL+Win if the 'imagesize' is changed while it contains an image? Changing 'Size' in Dyalog rescales the image.
⍝?      Answer (file): If using a bitmap file, the image is unscaled and centered. Increasing the imagesize causes it to be redrawn from the file, centered in the new size.
⍝?      Answer (graphics): Anything drawn on the picture is erased first.
⍝?      Note: Don't change 'Size' in Dyalog, change 'CBits' ⍴ instead, explicitly reconstructing as desired.
⍝? When changing Size in Dyalog, how does it interact with X/YRange and in what order should they be changed? -- Don't use Size
⍝? Does Dyalog re-scale Pictures when the Size changes even if the Picture definition is oversized and specified top-left alignment? -- Don't use Size
⍝? Can we change Size in Dyalog without rescaling what's in the image? -- Not needed, Win clears the window (must have a way to replicate) -- Don't use Size
⍝? Can Dyalog's 'File' property be changed any time? What about APL+Win's equivalent 'bitmap' property when using a file name? ⍝ Dyalog=Yes ⍝ Win=Yes, redrawn
